# This file ships with the boilerplate because the boilerplate becomes the
# project root, so it is in place before the first agent writes anything.
# A01 owns it (REQ-FND-13).
#
# Read the "never ignore" section at the bottom before adding a line. Two of the
# obvious entries in a JavaScript .gitignore would silently destroy this
# project's conformity evidence.

# ── Dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/releases

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
out/
dist/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ── Test and capture output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
test-results/
.playwright/
build/screenshots/*.tmp.png

# ── Secrets. These are the lines that matter ────────────────────────────────
# REQ-SEC-03 keeps secrets encrypted at rest; a committed .env makes that moot.
# The SMTP password, the OIDC client secret and the KEK all live here, and a
# git history is not something you can un-leak by deleting the file later.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!**/public/**/*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
secrets/

# ── Local and OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp

# ── Docker / runtime volumes ────────────────────────────────────────────────
docker/data/
docker/certs/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER ignore these. Each has been added to a .gitignore by mistake before,
# because each looks like build output and is not:
#
#   build/          The gate verdicts, the intake, the human's G1 approval and
#                   the cost ledger. compliance/cra/obligations-matrix.md cites
#                   build/gates/*.json as Annex I II(3) evidence at the strongest
#                   tier, on the grounds that an auditor can check a path. An
#                   auditor cannot check a path that is not in the repository.
#                   Only build/screenshots/*.tmp.png is ignored, above.
#   resources/      The pinned upstream baseline (REQ-UI-16), verified by
#                   resources/pin.json. Ignoring it turns the pin into a comment.
#   mockups/        The mockup sources are the reference the approved design is
#                   checked against (REQ-MOC-05). Their node_modules and .next
#                   are already covered by the patterns above.
#   packages/theme/fonts/   Self-hosted Montserrat (REQ-SUP-07). It is a binary
#                   asset, not a build artefact; fetching it at build time is
#                   the thing that requirement forbids.
#
# scripts/check-boilerplate.sh fails if any of them is ignored.
